	(text "Power tree: +5V is the TPS2116 power mux's output (U10), USB first, the console's 5 V second.\n  VBUS     USB-C (usb sheet) -> VIN1, the priority input: MODE on VIN1, PR1 from R35 33k / R36 10k, so VBUS\n           above VREF x 4.3 (3.96-4.64 V) runs the cart and the console's 7805 supplies nothing.\n  CONS_5V  edge 15, the console's 7805 -> VIN2, whenever VBUS is absent.\n  37-60 mOhm either way: +5V sits within ~20 mV of its source, so the 74HCT glue stays inside 4.5-5.5 V\n  on either; reverse current blocking: neither source back-feeds the other.  ST is not used.\n+5V feeds the 74HCT541 / '32 / '1G02 / '14, the WS2812, U12 AP2112K -> +3V3 (every RP2354B supply pin: it\nrises with +5V, so the 5 V-tolerant pads are never unpowered with 5 V on them) and U11 AP63203 -> +3V3_S3\n(the ESP32-S3, the CP2102N and the microSD; WiFi bursts ~400 mA; it waits out UVLO, then soft-starts over\n4 ms).  Console 5 V headroom under WiFi bursts is unmeasured: bring-up step 2.  TP14, TP13, TP15, TP16 and TP17 are\nbring-up pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
